1
00:00:00,059 --> 00:00:01,809
Welcome to Resgrid Academy.

2
00:00:02,190 --> 00:00:06,000
In this lesson, we will put the right
resgrid app on each device.

3
00:00:06,409 --> 00:00:09,880
A configured department still needs
members and shared devices to

4
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:13,060
sign in to the correct department with the
correct permissions.

5
00:00:13,439 --> 00:00:16,579
We will explain the features, the setup
decisions, and a

6
00:00:16,579 --> 00:00:18,479
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:19,010 --> 00:00:24,069
Members install the Responder app, a
tablet in Engine 1 runs the Unit app and

8
00:00:24,069 --> 00:00:26,029
a station screen shows the Big Board.

9
00:00:26,549 --> 00:00:29,150
Most members use Resgrid through the
Responder app.

10
00:00:29,589 --> 00:00:33,610
Getting everyone installed and signed in
is what lets dispatches reach them.

11
00:00:34,129 --> 00:00:37,540
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:37,540 --> 00:00:39,780
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:40,470 --> 00:00:41,760
Responder application.

14
00:00:42,229 --> 00:00:46,439
The member app for receiving dispatches,
responding and setting status.

15
00:00:46,889 --> 00:00:51,720
Have every member install the Responder
app, sign in and allow notifications.

16
00:00:52,349 --> 00:00:53,420
Unit application.

17
00:00:53,920 --> 00:00:56,770
The in-vehicle app that represents an
apparatus.

18
00:00:57,159 --> 00:01:01,459
Install the Unit app on each apparatus
tablet and select its unit.

19
00:01:02,079 --> 00:01:03,380
Dispatch application.

20
00:01:03,799 --> 00:01:06,770
The dispatcher view for creating and
managing calls.

21
00:01:07,159 --> 00:01:11,380
Give dispatch access to the people who
dispatch, then have them sign in.

22
00:01:12,199 --> 00:01:14,189
Incident command and accountability.

23
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:18,130
Incident command and accountability for
incident commanders.

24
00:01:18,659 --> 00:01:21,949
Give command access to the officers who
run incidents.

25
00:01:22,569 --> 00:01:23,229
Big Board.

26
00:01:23,689 --> 00:01:26,869
A station display of calls, units and
personnel.

27
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:30,829
Open the Big Board on a station screen and
choose what it shows.

28
00:01:31,499 --> 00:01:32,130
Dashboard.

29
00:01:32,619 --> 00:01:36,759
The department home page: current status,
staffing and activity.

30
00:01:37,169 --> 00:01:40,549
Decide which devices each role will use
and share the app

31
00:01:40,549 --> 00:01:42,150
download links with your members.

32
00:01:42,749 --> 00:01:43,659
My Profile.

33
00:01:44,050 --> 00:01:48,009
Your own profile, contact details and
notification preferences.

34
00:01:48,370 --> 00:01:51,740
Decide which devices each role will use
and share the app

35
00:01:51,740 --> 00:01:53,299
download links with your members.

36
00:01:53,969 --> 00:01:54,949
Your Departments.

37
00:01:55,360 --> 00:01:57,389
Switch between the departments you belong
to.

38
00:01:57,929 --> 00:02:01,370
Decide which devices each role will use
and share the app

39
00:02:01,370 --> 00:02:02,959
download links with your members.

40
00:02:03,599 --> 00:02:06,299
For the training scenario, work in this
order.

41
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:07,309
Step 1.

42
00:02:07,869 --> 00:02:11,539
Set up a member device with Responder and
notification permissions.

43
00:02:11,970 --> 00:02:12,689
Step 2.

44
00:02:13,130 --> 00:02:16,510
Set up an apparatus tablet with Unit and
select its unit.

45
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:17,640
Step 3.

46
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:22,630
Grant appropriate Dispatch or Command
access and configure a station Big Board.

47
00:02:23,370 --> 00:02:24,730
Now verify the result.

48
00:02:25,249 --> 00:02:28,469
Check the active department, device
identity, and a

49
00:02:28,510 --> 00:02:30,110
controlled notification test.

50
00:02:30,590 --> 00:02:32,950
Check what a shared station screen
exposes.

51
00:02:33,469 --> 00:02:38,230
A common problem to watch for: Installing
an app does not prove alerts arrive.

52
00:02:38,730 --> 00:02:43,210
Verify OS notification and location
settings on the actual device used.

53
00:02:43,939 --> 00:02:45,509
Your practice task is simple.

54
00:02:45,909 --> 00:02:50,390
Use a sample member, unit tablet,
dispatcher, and station display to

55
00:02:50,390 --> 00:02:52,209
follow the same training incident.

56
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:54,909
Record which devices complete the test.

57
00:02:55,270 --> 00:02:59,220
Record the result, who owns the follow-up,
and when it should be reviewed.

58
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:02,949
Use the linked feature scripts for the
detailed screen recording plan.

